---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import MermaidDiagram from '../components/MermaidDiagram.astro';
import { agentInteractionDiagram } from '../data/diagrams';
---

<DocsLayout title="Sub-Agents" sectionLabel="How It Works" activeSlug="agents">

  <div class="panel-intro">
    <h2>Sub-Agents</h2>
    <p>Instead of one AI doing everything, VibeCrew splits work across <strong>specialized agents</strong> &mdash; like a real development team with planners, builders, testers, and reviewers. Most agents run on Opus, the most powerful model available. This is intentional: while Opus costs more per task and takes longer, the higher quality output means significantly less rework. Getting it right the first time saves more time and money than running a cheaper model that needs multiple correction rounds. Fast, mechanical tasks (routing, running shell commands) use Haiku, and template-driven output like documentation uses Sonnet.</p>
    <div class="key-points">
      <div class="key-point">
        <span class="key-icon purple">&#9632;</span>
        <div>
          <strong>What they are</strong>
          <p>AI specialists with scoped tool access, model selection, and turn budgets. Most run on Opus (the most capable model) because planning, coding, security, and analysis are tasks where mistakes are expensive to fix later. Haiku handles fast mechanical work, and Sonnet handles documentation.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="key-point">
        <span class="key-icon green">&#10003;</span>
        <div>
          <strong>What problem they solve</strong>
          <p>A single AI context window fills up fast when researching, coding, and testing in one session. Worktree agents offload expensive research into isolated contexts &mdash; only the distilled output enters your main session, saving thousands of tokens.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h4 class="agent-table-heading">Agent Reference</h4>
  <div class="agent-legend">
    <span class="legend-item"><span class="legend-dot" style="background:var(--color-accent)"></span> Opus (complex reasoning)</span>
    <span class="legend-item"><span class="legend-dot" style="background:var(--color-amber)"></span> Haiku (fast tasks)</span>
    <span class="legend-item"><span class="legend-dot" style="background:var(--color-blue)"></span> Sonnet (documentation)</span>
  </div>
  <div class="agent-table-wrap">
    <table class="agent-table">
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Agent</th><th>Model</th><th>Isolation</th><th>Memory</th><th>What It Does</th><th>Triggered By</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Session Startup</strong></td>
          <td><span class="badge amber">Haiku</span></td>
          <td>Inline</td>
          <td>—</td>
          <td>Environment check, state detection, handoff detection, routing</td>
          <td>Every session start</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Workflow Orchestrator</strong></td>
          <td><span class="badge opus">Opus</span></td>
          <td>Inline</td>
          <td>—</td>
          <td>Routes between Tier 1 and Tier 2, coordinates agent handoffs, manages backlog</td>
          <td>Command routing</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Stack Scout</strong></td>
          <td><span class="badge opus">Opus</span></td>
          <td>Worktree</td>
          <td>—</td>
          <td>Read-only research via WebSearch, Context7, Chrome DevTools. Produces TDR</td>
          <td>Tier 1 architecture step</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Builder</strong></td>
          <td><span class="badge opus">Opus</span></td>
          <td>Worktree</td>
          <td>Expertise</td>
          <td>Creates implementation plans, generates ASCII wireframes, implements features: component selection, code generation, accessibility and visual verification</td>
          <td>Tier 2 plan + design + code phases</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Verifier</strong></td>
          <td><span class="badge amber">Haiku</span></td>
          <td>Inline</td>
          <td>—</td>
          <td>Runs tests, lint, build, and type-check. Reports pass/fail results</td>
          <td><code>/check</code>, <code>/wrap</code>, <code>/run-backlog</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Performance Coach</strong></td>
          <td><span class="badge opus">Opus</span></td>
          <td>Inline</td>
          <td>Project</td>
          <td>Cross-session trend analysis, anti-pattern detection, CLAUDE.md mutation proposals</td>
          <td><code>/wrap</code> session end</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Code Auditor</strong></td>
          <td><span class="badge opus">Opus</span></td>
          <td>Worktree</td>
          <td>—</td>
          <td>Read-only codebase analysis for existing project onboarding</td>
          <td><code>/onboard</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Security Auditor</strong></td>
          <td><span class="badge opus">Opus</span></td>
          <td>Worktree</td>
          <td>Project</td>
          <td>OWASP Top 10 security analysis: injection, auth, XSS, secrets</td>
          <td><code>/audit</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Doc Generator</strong></td>
          <td><span class="badge sonnet">Sonnet</span></td>
          <td>Inline</td>
          <td>—</td>
          <td>Feature docs, CHANGELOG, release notes, VitePress sidebar regeneration</td>
          <td><code>/wrap</code>, Tier 2 docs phase</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Code Simplifier</strong></td>
          <td><span class="badge opus">Opus</span></td>
          <td>Worktree</td>
          <td>Project</td>
          <td>Dead code detection, abstraction flattening, API surface reduction</td>
          <td><code>/simplify</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>CI Healer</strong></td>
          <td><span class="badge opus">Opus</span></td>
          <td>Inline</td>
          <td>—</td>
          <td>CI failure diagnosis and repair. Categorizes failures, max 3 fix attempts</td>
          <td><code>/heal</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Opponent Processor</strong></td>
          <td><span class="badge opus">Opus</span></td>
          <td>Worktree</td>
          <td>—</td>
          <td>Devil's advocate for TDR decisions: counter-arguments, debate matrices, risks</td>
          <td>Tier 1 after TDR</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Code Reviewer</strong></td>
          <td><span class="badge opus">Opus</span></td>
          <td>Worktree</td>
          <td>Expertise</td>
          <td>Read-only code review against feature spec, TDR compliance, conventions</td>
          <td><code>/review</code>, <code>/run-backlog</code></td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>System Reviewer</strong></td>
          <td><span class="badge opus">Opus</span></td>
          <td>Worktree</td>
          <td>—</td>
          <td>Plugin meta-analysis, cross-project telemetry, ecosystem research</td>
          <td><code>/system-review</code></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h4 class="agent-table-heading">Shared Helpers</h4>
  <p class="cmd-group-desc">
    Agents share common procedures via <code>agents/helpers.md</code> &mdash; a centralized reference file with named sections for registration, profile reading, budget discipline, and more. This avoids duplicating the same instructions across 14 agent files, reducing prompt size and maintenance overhead.
  </p>
  <div class="agent-table-wrap">
    <table class="agent-table">
      <thead><tr><th>Helper</th><th>Agents</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>#Registration</code></td><td>All 14</td><td>Observability tracking on agent start</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>#Read-User-Profile</code></td><td>9</td><td>Profile-aware output adaptation</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>#Read-Only-Agent-Constraints</code></td><td>8</td><td>Enforce no-write safety for analysis agents</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>#Budget-Discipline</code></td><td>All 14</td><td>Context window management</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>#Escalation-on-Max-Turns</code></td><td>5</td><td>Graceful partial output on turn limit</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>#Expertise-Integration</code></td><td>3</td><td>Cross-session knowledge accumulation</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <MermaidDiagram chart={agentInteractionDiagram} caption="Agent topology: how agents hand off work to each other" />

</DocsLayout>
